# eci_virtual_machine_allocation (Resource)

Manages an ECI virtual machine allocation. Controls whether a VM is running.

- **Create** this resource to **start** the VM.
- **Destroy** this resource to **stop** the VM (the VM itself and all attached resources are preserved).

This is separate from [`eci_virtual_machine`](virtual_machine) because creating a VM only defines its spec. The allocation controls whether the VM is actually running.

!> **WARNING:** Avoid stopping a VM immediately after starting it. If the OS is still booting, the graceful shutdown signal may not be processed, causing the termination to take significantly longer.

